<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - Stocks Hotels EPS 21 cts.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Stocks Hotels EPS 21 cts.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended April 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - attrib		  21.0 (in line with forecast made at</p>
<p>time of listing in February 1997)</p>
<p>    Maiden div (cts)	3.0</p>
<p>    Net income		9.67</p>
<p>    Operating income	13.78</p>
<p>    Associates earnings   3.42</p>
<p>    Net interest	    3.31</p>
<p>    Turnover		  59.33</p>
<p>    Retained income	 13.08</p>
<p>Div payable Aug 29</p>
<p>on register Aug 15</p>
<p>Full name: Stocks Hotels and Resorts Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - No comparative figures have been shown as this is the company's first year of operations.</p>
<p>The company said two licence applications for casinos have been submitted in Gauteng, the outcome of which is expected by year-end. The group has further plans to bid for casino licences in the Western Cape and KwaZulu Natal.</p>
<p>While crime is expected to affect marketing, the group's hotels will continue to gain market share particularly from international visitors, it said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
